    file: "web-research-guide.md",
    content: "# A-Z of Web Research\n\nA short course in finding, judging and citing sources online. Work through the\nvideos first, then use the Purdue OWL sections as reference while you write.\n\n## Start with technique\n\n1. **How to skim internet articles** - a practical method for deciding within a\n   minute whether a source is worth reading.\n   <https://youtu.be/iuCRDeUYXww>\n\n2. **Evaluating and validating research sources** - how to tell a credible\n   source from a confident one.\n   <https://youtu.be/FKaH7PlXx1Q>\n\n## Plan the research\n\n3. **Research: where to begin** - choosing a topic, narrowing it and building a\n   research question before you search.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/research_overview/index.html>\n\n4. **Conducting primary research** - interviews, surveys, observation and\n   experiments, and when each is appropriate.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/conducting_primary_research/index.html>\n\n## Judge what you find\n\n5. **Evaluating sources of information** - bibliographic evaluation, reading\n   evaluation, print versus internet sources and evaluating web sources.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/evaluating_sources_of_information/index.html>\n\n6. **Web research** - search engines, Boolean operators, web directories and the\n   invisible web, with an annotated links section.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/searching_online/index.html>\n\n7. **Internet references** - dictionaries, style manuals, grammar handbooks,\n   editing resources, indexes for writers, online libraries and e-texts,\n   newspapers, journals and magazines.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/internet_references/index.html>\n\n## Work in the archives\n\n8. **Archival research** - conducting research in different kinds of archives,\n   with the considerations and best practice for each.\n   <https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/research_and_citation/conducting_research/archival_research/index.html>\n\n## Before you cite a source, check\n\n- Who wrote it, and what are their qualifications?\n- Is it primary evidence, reporting or opinion?\n- When was it published or last updated?\n- Does it cite sources you can follow?\n- Is it published by a university, government, journal or recognised institution?\n\nSourced from the A-Z of Web Research guide.\n",
